  "attestation": "D-133 (owner 2026-11-03): the questions alembic_needs.mjs export hands to Alembic are worded for the instructor. New scripts/lib/core/needs_wording.mjs (presentation only): places named as the instructor sees them (course map; concept map, assessment guide, study guide, slides or practice questions for a chapter by title; a passage by its first words; plan-node ids as the plan words), content quoted as it reads (orz markup, plan annotations, maths, mhchem, sub/superscripts rendered to plain text), one sentence on what is wrong and one on the suggestion per digest kind; harness notes lose paths, lines, decision codes, unit/node ids, spine and commands, while a reviewer words are only rendered. alembic_needs.mjs: digestQuestion takes a wording context (needsContext: titles, plan nodes, unit places and text); interrupts, M5, approvals and corrections are worded the same way; the harness wording and its codes are kept as each question assistant entry in private/coursewerk/digest/alembic-needs.json, never in the hand-in, whose fields and limits are unchanged (Alembic agent-runtime-v3 section 22; Alembic parseDigest and the Needs-you view read unchanged). Choices: Apply the suggestion / Keep it / Later (apply is ms8-verdicts acceptance) for knowledge concerns and clarifications with a suggestion, spine-review concerns with a suggestion and detail in the plan; Keep it / Drop it / Later for off-plan passages; DIGEST_CHOICES kinds unchanged; digest choices still require words; a reviewer suggestion is never recommended. No finding, evidence, basis, key, apply path or answer meaning changed (the test checks each asked entry carries its finding evidence unchanged and that Apply the suggestion records an /^apply/ choice). Tests: tests/alembic-needs-wording.test.mjs added (every question kind on the real C2 package: no path, line, code or markup in text, detail or choices; refs and hidden codes kept; answers mean what they meant), tests/alembic-needs.test.mjs updated for the new wording (M5 label, a choice answer to the detail-in-spine question, the diff detail as plain text). req.host.alembic-needs-wording added, req.host.alembic-needs-export choices clause amended; README, alembic-job/CLAUDE.md and CHANGELOG (Unreleased) updated; VERSION unchanged. Reviewed every required item; the others do not describe question wording or the needs record. Tests: the 36 required tests plus alembic-needs, alembic-needs-wording and job-release: 576 passed, 0 failed (COURSEWERK_FRAMES=installed, concurrency 2, one test process).",
